[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Pawn Game"]
[Variation "King's Pawn Game: Wayward Queen Attack"]
[ECO "C20"]
[Character "solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "early-queen,mate-threat"]
[Themes "tempo-on-queen,f7-defence"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2.Qh5"]
[Start "giuoco-piano 1...e5"]

2. Qh5 { The queen comes out on move two. It hits e5 and eyes f7, but it breaks the rule of developing the minor pieces first, so Black can chase it. } 2... Nc6 { Guards e5 and develops with a piece that the queen cannot hit. } 3. Bc4 { Queen and bishop both aim at f7. Qxf7 would be checkmate. } ( 3. Bb5 Nf6 { Develops with a hit on the queen. The bishop on b5 does nothing for White's attack. } ) ( 3. Nf3 Nf6 { Develops with a hit on the queen, which must move again. } ) 3... g6 { Attacks the queen and, once it moves, Black can develop in peace. Never play 3...Nf6, which lets White play Qxf7 mate. } 4. Qf3 { Keeps the pressure on f7. } 4... Nf6 { Develops and blocks the f-file, so the queen cannot reach f7. } 5. Ne2 ( 5. c3 Bg7 ) ( 5. d3 Nd4 { Attacks the queen and c2 at once. The queen has to leave f3. } 6. Qd1 d5 ) ( 5. Nc3 Nd4 6. Qd1 c6 { Prepares ...d5, which would hit the bishop and take the centre. } ) ( 5. Nh3 Nd4 6. Qd1 d5 ) 5... Bg7 { Develops the bishop. } 6. d3 O-O 7. Nbc3 d6 { Protects e5 and opens the c8 bishop. } 8. a3 h6 { Stops a bishop or knight from landing on g5 and bothering the kingside. } 9. Bd2 Kh7 { Black has developed fully while White's queen wandered. Plan: ...Be6 to trade White's attacking bishop, then ...Qd7 and ...Rae8. } *
